't relapse or anything because he  tends to sit in the chair outside the  perimeter of the group and seldom  participate himself that is until one  meeting in March of 2007 when a man  named Bobby dagen attends the group as  part of a press tour for his book  survive my story of overcoming jigsaw  dr. Gordon sees just one issue with this  publication he knows full well that  Bobby dagen was never one of the jigsaw  victims so he calls him out on it and  what is probably my favorite scene  involving dr. Gordon let's roll it  [Music]  markable if not a little perverse I'm  sure I speak for everyone here when I  say how grateful we are to be part of  your promotional  vd that's hilarious and I love how the  camera operator is just like oh we got  to get this and then everybody who  starts clapping that's remarkable but  Lawrence continues to keep a watchful  eye over Jill tuck and of course her  enemy mark Hoffman on March 12 2007  Hoffman is finally able to catch up with  an exact his revenge on Jill  which means Gordon is obligated to act  immediately Hoffman packs a bag of  supplies and sets fire to his savings  before setting out to make his escape  but he's met with three people in pig  masks were led by dr. Lawrence Gordon it  would seem that Gordon has taken a page  from his master and acquired a couple  disciples of his own he follows Jon's  instructions to leave Hoffman in the  location that means the most in the  place where he overcame jigsaws trial  the dilapidated bathroom but Hoffman is  not given the same option that he had  two-and-a-half years ago he pulls the  last remaining hacksaw out of Hoffman's  reach and throws it out of the room  leaving him to die and fulfilling his  teacher's final request  this would leave Gordon as the only  living true successor to jigsaw and  that's the exciting part about his  character in 2016 a forgotten disciple  from John Kramer's past a man named  Logan Nelson re-emerges and uses the  jigsaw name to get revenge on a cop that  had wronged him and many others while  this man was trained by Kramer at one  time he is strayed from his ideals in  the same way that Hoffman did at the  time of recording were yet to see how  dr. Gordon reacts to this but I imagine  based on everything that we know about  him that he's still keeping a watchful  eye and probably not too happy about  Logan Nelson causing his old master to  be dug up from his grave after having  his legacy altered in a negative way  like this so it'll be interesting to see  if dr. Gordon decides to intervene  John's intention from the very beginning  with dr. Gordon was to make him cherish  his life by reintroducing passion  originally that is intended to be  passion for his family Alison and Diana  it's never canonically shown what  happens to his wife and daughter but in  an audio commentary on saw 7 it stated  that they got divorced after Alison saw  how Lawrence had changed following the  bathroom game there's nothing in the  films to contradict that and it does  make sense because they aren't present  at the support group but we can't say  for sure until there's some evidence in  a future film  but what we can say is that passion was  reintroduced into Lawrence's life  anyways because he became passionate  about jigsaws teachings and helping  people improve their lives using his  methods this causes him to become the  only one of jigsaws apprentices to  become a true heir to John's vision of  what jigsaw could be and it'll be fun to  see how this new jigsaw continues with  the spirit of John's teachings going  forward let me know in the comments  though who else would you like to see  covered here on horror history I've  already got a playlist on the left of  the histories of other saw characters so  be sure to check those out and remember  to subscribe to seize these world for  new Horrors every week bring that DEATH  BATTLE for notifications and I'll see  you in the next one assuming we both  survive  you  [Music]
 

